Apple designed <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI on the HomeView to complete household tasks with natural voice commands and minimal follow-up questions, executives told <a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1011431/apple-homeview-smart-display-best-feature"><em>The Verge</em></a>, emphasizing simplicity as a key feature of the new home hub.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/homeview-calendar.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070340" /><br/>
In an new interview, Kaiann Drance, Apple's vice president of product marketing for home, linked the timing of HomeView's introduction to &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI's personal context capabilities and Apple's approach to privacy.<br/>
<br/>
"With the magic of &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI, it comes together in a way that we haven't been able to deliver before," Drance said.<br/>
<br/>
Lilian Rincon, Apple's vice president of product marketing for AI, described &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI as "much more capable," highlighting how conversational requests could make smart home accessories easier to control:<br/>
<br/>
<blockquote>It's great because you can just ask it to change the temperature on your thermostat in a very natural way. As the Siri AI capabilities continue to evolve, the home experience is fitting to be able to interact with in this natural way.</blockquote><br/>
<br/>
Rincon said that allowing people to speak naturally broadens the audience for the technology:<br/>
<br/>
<blockquote>Because now it can be my mother-in-law or the Gen Z who's in college, both of them can use this in the way that they naturally speak and get what they want.</blockquote><br/>
<br/>
Apple's approach apparently also places emphasis on limiting the exchanges needed to complete a task. Rincon said the assistant is designed to act on a request and let the user move on:<br/>
<br/>
<blockquote>A lot of these assistants out there are always asking questions because they want more information. For us, it isn't about that. We're there to get it done, take an action for you, show you what you need to get done, and then really get out of the way.</blockquote><br/>
<br/>
HomeView can recognize up to six people and display information tailored to each user. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; requests involving personal context <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/homeview-needs-an-iphone-for-some-ai-features/">require a paired device</a> that supports <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a>. General knowledge questions, natural conversations, and improved music discovery are still available without an Apple Intelligence-compatible iPhone or <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a>.<br/>
<br/>
